db.articles.createSearchIndex({
name: "default",
definition: {
mappings: {
dynamic: false,
fields: {
title: { type: "string", analyzer: "lucene.standard" },
body: { type: "string", analyzer: "lucene.english" },
tags: { type: "string", analyzer: "keyword" },
created: { type: "date" }
}
}
}
})
dynamic: true auto-indexes every string field; useful for prototyping, costly at scale.

db.articles.aggregate([
{ $search: {
index: "default",
text: {
query: "mongodb tutorial",
path: ["title", "body"],
fuzzy: { maxEdits: 1 }
}
}},
{ $project: { _id: 1, title: 1, score: { $meta: "searchScore" } } },
{ $limit: 20 }
])
Compound queries with must / should / mustNot / filter:
{ $search: {
index: "default",
compound: {
must: [{ text: { query: "mongo", path: "body" } }],
should: [{ text: { query: "atlas", path: "title", score: { boost: { value: 3 } } } }],
filter: [{ range: { path: "created", gte: ISODate("2026-01-01") } }],
mustNot: [{ text: { query: "deprecated", path: "tags" } }]
}
}}

{ $searchMeta: {
index: "default",
facet: {
operator: { text: { query: "mongo", path: "body" } },
facets: {
tag_facet: { type: "string", path: "tags" },
year_facet: { type: "date", path: "created", boundaries: [ISODate("2024"), ISODate("2025"), ISODate("2026")] }
}
}
}}
Produces counts per facet bucket — perfect for filtered search UIs.

{ $search: {
index: "default",
autocomplete: {
query: "mongo",
path: "title",
fuzzy: { maxEdits: 1 }
}
}}
Add an autocomplete field type in the index definition (type: "autocomplete").
Atlas Search replaces $text (Post 02) for any serious search workload — scoring, autocomplete, fuzzy, facets, multi-language, synonyms.

db.documents.createSearchIndex({
name: "vector_index",
type: "vectorSearch",
definition: {
fields: [
{
type: "vector",
path: "embedding",
numDimensions: 1536, // matches your embedding model
similarity: "cosine" // cosine | euclidean | dotProduct
},
{
type: "filter",
path: "category" // can filter alongside vector search
}
]
}
})
The index is HNSW (Hierarchical Navigable Small World) under the hood — fast approximate nearest neighbour at scale.

db.documents.aggregate([
{ $vectorSearch: {
index: "vector_index",
path: "embedding",
queryVector: [/* 1536-dim float array from your embedder */],
numCandidates: 200, // search width (recall vs latency trade-off)
limit: 10,
filter: { category: "tech" } // optional pre-filter
}},
{ $project: { _id: 1, title: 1, score: { $meta: "vectorSearchScore" } } }
])

